  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while both image-only baselines (config_010, config_013) are far weaker at ~21-23%, indicating RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multiprofile representation with aggregation improves over singleprofile, and no data on any aggregation method. This experiment (config_002) directly extends config_001 by switching to multiprofile + avgpool while keeping the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), cleanly isolating the effect of profile structure and aggregation. Choosing avgpool over transformer first is the simpler, more conservative test: if multiprofile+avgpool helps, we can then test transformer as a refinement; if it does not, the multiprofile structure itself is ruled out as the bottleneck, redirecting attention to encoder choice. Under a tight budget, this single-variable change from the best existing baseline maximizes information gained per experiment."
}

